{"id":"7ec6587325c977aedfe66046d2ca859291f0835a","axis":"silent","repo":"systemd/systemd","sha":"7ec6587325c977aedfe66046d2ca859291f0835a","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/TRANSIENT-SETTINGS.md","lines":["@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@ Most generic unit settings are available for transient units."," "," ```"," ✓ Description=","+✓ Tags="," ✓ SourcePath="," ✓ OnFailureJobMode="," ✓ JobTimeoutAction="],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"man/org.freedesktop.systemd1.xml","lines":["@@ -2107,6 +2107,16 @@ node /org/freedesktop/systemd1 {","       state require <interfacename>org.freedesktop.systemd1.bypass-dump-ratelimit</interfacename> to avoid","       rate limits.","       </para>","+","+      <para>The <interfacename>org.freedesktop.systemd1.manage-units</interfacename> polkit action may sometimes","+      pass some additional variables that can be used by polkit policies for more precise targeting. The","+      <literal>unit</literal> variable may be set to the name of the systemd unit being managed. The <literal>verb</literal>","+      variable may be set to the specific action being performed. Units that have <varname>Tags</varname>","+      configured will also expose the tags: parameterized tags will be prefixed with <literal>tag.</literal>","+      and their value will be the variable's value, and un-parameterized tags will be prefixed with <literal>btag.</literal>","+      and the variable's value will be <literal>1</literal>. For instance, a unit tagged with <literal>example=value</literal>","+      and <literal>otherexample</literal> will have the <literal>tag.example</literal> variable set to","+      <literal>value</literal> and the <literal>btag.otherexample</literal> variable set to <literal>1</literal>.</para>","     </refsect2>","   </refsect1>"," ","@@ -2226,6 +2236,8 @@ node /org/freedesktop/systemd1/unit/avahi_2ddaemon_2eservice {","       @org.freedesktop.DBus.Property.EmitsChangedSignal(\"const\")","       readonly s Description = '...';","